win10xbox: kernelbase exports what the genuine user32/imm32 import through the host API-set map

The guest shares the host PEB, so ApiSetMap is Windows' own schema: api-ms-win-core-heap-obsolete
resolves to kernelbase (Wine: kernel32), and the native user32/imm32 import CheckTokenMembershipEx,
SetProcessValidCallTargets and the Global*/Local* family from there. Wine had the first two as stubs and
the rest only in kernel32, so the loader bound a stub that raised EXCEPTION_WINE_STUB (the Global*/Local*
ones now forward to kernel32). Applies on top of 0003.

